{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team doctors. I understand you came in after having your nephrostomy tube replaced this morning and then developed some pain and chills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. Right after I got home, I had this sharp pain in my lower belly that went to my right side. And I’ve been feeling feverish and nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You also mentioned some burning when you urinate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, since the tube was changed. It wasn’t like that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history with the transplanted kidney and the recent procedure, we’re concerned about a possible infection. We’ve started you on an antibiotic called linezolid just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of the tube change? I was worried something went wrong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common after procedures like this. The manipulation can introduce bacteria. We’re being cautious because you’ve had infections before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. My daughter said I’ve seemed really down lately. I just feel so tired of being in and out of the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. We actually spoke with your daughter, and we’ve requested a psychiatry consult to help support you emotionally during this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’d really like to talk to someone. My grandson is in the NICU, and I feel like I’m not even helping my family right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-01-07 22:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a lot to carry. We’ll make sure you get the support you need. For now, let’s focus on getting the infection under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your urine culture came back — it shows E. coli, which is a common bacteria. The good news is it’s not resistant, so we can switch you to a different antibiotic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I’ve heard of E. coli from food poisoning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s the same bacteria, but here it’s causing a urinary tract infection. Since you have a stent and tube, it can travel up more easily. We’ll treat it with cefpodoxime, an oral antibiotic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to stay in the hospital for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you a bit longer to make sure the fever doesn’t come back and that you’re tolerating the medication. Your white blood cell count is normal, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-01-08 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The new antibiotic made me a little nauseous earlier. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-01-08 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Actually, that might be from another medication — atovaquone. It’s for pneumonia prevention, but it can cause nausea. We’re switching you to dapsone instead, which should be easier on your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-01-08 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I was worried I was reacting badly to everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-01-08 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. We’re adjusting based on how you respond. Your kidney function is stable — creatinine is 2.2, and today it’s down to 2.1. That’s a good trend."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed some leakage around your nephrostomy tube again. That’s not ideal — it can increase infection risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s been dripping more since yesterday. Is the tube loose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Imaging suggests the stent may have shifted. We recommend replacing the tube again to ensure proper drainage and stop the leak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another procedure? Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a quick procedure under light sedation. You’ll be comfortable. We’ll use imaging to guide it and make sure the new tube is placed correctly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. I just want this to stop happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you did great this morning. The tube was replaced successfully. The old one had migrated — the pigtail wasn’t in the right place, which caused the leak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why it wasn’t working right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The new one is positioned well — contrast showed good flow into the bladder and no leakage. That should help prevent more infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I’ve been so worried about getting sick again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are too. That’s why we’re being thorough. Your latest labs look good — creatinine is now 1.9, which is your baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-01-10 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The psychiatrist came by earlier. It helped just to talk. They said I’m coping well, considering everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-01-10 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m really glad you spoke with them. Emotional health is part of your recovery. We’ll make sure you have follow-up support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re doing well. No fever, eating normally, and the tube isn’t leaking. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the tube open to gravity drainage and record your output daily. Call the transplant office if you have fever, increased pain, redness, or less urine from the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue your usual doses — tacrolimus, mycophenolate, warfarin, and the others. Plus, the new antibiotic cefpodoxime for 10 days, and dapsone instead of atovaquone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to take them. Should I watch for any side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "With dapsone, watch for rash or shortness of breath — but it’s usually well-tolerated. The antibiotic might cause mild stomach upset. Take it with food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my weight — I’ve lost a few pounds. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve lost about 4 pounds since discharge, but your kidney function is stable. Keep monitoring it. If you keep losing weight or feel weaker, let us know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I just want to get back to feeling normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on the right track. The transplant team will follow up with your tacrolimus levels. And keep in touch with your counselor — your mental health matters just as much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate how you’ve explained everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. We’re here to support you. A nurse will go over your discharge instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another tube change soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not immediately. We’ll monitor you. The goal is to keep it stable. If there are no leaks or infections, you may go several weeks before the next one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds manageable. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have you out soon. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Rest well, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make the appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better knowing what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we aim for. Knowledge helps you take control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep recording my outputs and call if anything seems off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re doing a great job managing your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for not rushing me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You deserve the time. We’re a team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2156-01-11 07:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel like I can handle this now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2156-01-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. Stay in touch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2156-01-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2156-01-11 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2156-01-11 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-01-07 21:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-01-11 13:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with symptoms of urinary tract infection following a nephrostomy tube and stent replacement, including low-grade fever, chills, nausea, and flank pain. She was started on linezolid for presumed infection, and urine cultures later confirmed E. coli, leading to a switch to oral cefpodoxime. Leakage around the tube persisted, prompting a second tube replacement, after which drainage improved and symptoms resolved. Her kidney function stabilized with creatinine returning to baseline. A psychiatry consult addressed her emotional distress related to recurrent hospitalizations and family stress, and she was transitioned from atovaquone to dapsone due to nausea. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to monitor nephrostomy output, continue antibiotics, and follow up with the transplant and mental health teams.",
    "problems": [
      "Urinary complications, not elsewhere classified",
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Bacteremia",
      "Other mechanical complication of genitourinary device, implant, and graft",
      "Stricture or kinking of ureter",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other parts of uterus",
      "Escherichia coli [E. coli] infection in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site"
    ]
  }
}
